  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 116 AM CDT Wed Aug 19 2026\n\nThe forecast pattern continues to be fairly stagnant, with small \nshifts in the center position of the mid-level high. Hot and \ngenerally dry conditions will persist through the forecast, though \nthere is a very low chance for some seabreeze convection. \n\nWe have noticed that the forecast high temperatures have been a bit \nlower than we have been reaching so, with no significant change to \nthe pattern, have blended the observed max temperatures with the \nmost recent NBM (75/25) over land. Temperatures are expected to \nrange from 90 along the coast to around 105 inland, keeping us in a \nmoderate to high HeatRisk. Heat index values over the Coastal Bend \nwill reach 110-113, so have issued a Heat Advisory for this \nafternoon. More telling, the WetBulb Glob Temperatures (based on \nTexas UIL guidelines) are expected to be Moderate today, so it is \nimportant to take at least 4 separate 5 minute breaks out of the \nsun/heat. Drink plenty of water and/or electrolytes, dress in light, \nloose clothing, and make sure you monitor yourself and others for \nheat exhaustion.",
